# scope-bin was the ONE artifact missing from this list, and that omission is exactly how a
# 3.1 MB ELF executable got committed (2026-09-17, found when `make clean` in the S2 axis
# sweep deleted a TRACKED file). An enumerated ignore list fails open: a Makefile target
# added later is not covered by anything, and nothing objects. Same shape as the root
# `**/bin/` allowlist that swallowed `forth`'s entrypoint, in the opposite direction --
# there an omission hid a source file, here it published a binary.
scope-bin
*.pc
